+# The Daily Grind
+
+Run `pnpm install` and `pnpm start`. The server uses port 11222 by default;
+set `PORT` to override it.
+
+The server sends a `Permissions-Policy` header allowing this app's origin to
+request resources on the user's local network and loopback interface. It also
+includes the legacy `local-network-access` directive for older browsers.
+
+In production, serve the app over HTTPS. Users must grant any local-network
+permissions requested by their browser, and local services must allow the app's
+origin through CORS when the app reads cross-origin responses. Requests must run
+in the user's browser so that loopback addresses refer to their device.
+
+If the app is embedded in a cross-origin iframe, the parent must also delegate
+these permissions using the iframe's `allow` attribute:
+
+```html
+allow="local-network; loopback-network; local-network-access"
+```
+
+Any production host or reverse proxy serving the HTML must preserve the header
+configured in `server.mjs` (or configure the same header itself).
